{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Jack McElhone (born 1993) is a former Scottish child and teenage actor.","title":"Jack McElhone"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is famous for his role as Frankie in the 2004 film "Dear Frankie", for which he was nominated for a BAFTA Scotland Award.","title":"Jack McElhone"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He also had roles in "Young Adam", "The Book Group", "Stacked" and Nowhere Boy.","title":"Jack McElhone"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Dear Frankie is a 2004 British drama film directed by Shona Auerbach and starring Emily Mortimer, Gerard Butler, and Jack McElhone.","title":"Dear Frankie"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The screenplay by Andrea Gibb focuses on a young single mother whose love for her son prompts her to perpetuate a deception designed to protect him from the truth about his father.","title":"Dear Frankie"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Erich Bergen (born December 31, 1985) is an American actor and presenter, perhaps best known for his role as Bob Gaudio in the biographical musical drama film "Jersey Boys".","title":"Erich Bergen"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Tin Pan Alley Rag is a 2009 biographical musical play produced by The Roundabout Theatre Company.","title":"The Tin Pan Alley Rag"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The play set in 1915 is about Irving Berlin and Scott Joplin and their careers at the Tin Pan Alley in New York City is written by Mark Saltzman and directed by Stafford Arima.","title":"The Tin Pan Alley Rag"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Nowhere Boy is a 2009 British biographical musical drama film about John Lennon's adolescence, his relationships with his aunt Mimi Smith and his mother Julia Lennon, the creation of his first band, the Quarrymen, and its evolution into the Beatles.","title":"Nowhere Boy"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film is based on a biography written by Lennon's half-sister Julia Baird.","title":"Nowhere Boy"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The film received its US release on 8 October 2010, coinciding with that weekend's celebrations of the 70th anniversary of Lennon's birth (9 October 1940).","title":"Nowhere Boy"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Jersey Boys is a 2014 American biographical musical drama film directed and produced by Clint Eastwood based on the Tony Award winning jukebox musical of the same name.","title":"Jersey Boys (film)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film tells the story of the musical group The Four Seasons.","title":"Jersey Boys (film)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The film was released in the United States on June 20, 2014.","title":"Jersey Boys (film)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $67 million worldwide.","title":"Jersey Boys (film)"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Nowhere Boy
